      "traceTextDiagram": "Human sends message to agent (Trace 1)\n├── CLI Command Entry\n│   └── foxctl-mail main() \u003c-- 1a\n│       └── sendMessage() \u003c-- cmd/foxctl-mail/main.go:133\n│           ├── Load config \u003c-- cmd/foxctl-mail/main.go:134\n│           ├── OpenBoardStore() \u003c-- 1b\n│           └── store.SendMessage() \u003c-- 1c\n│               └── BoardStore.SendMessage() \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:62\n│                   ├── Generate ULID \u0026 defaults \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:63\n│                   └── SQL INSERT board_messages \u003c-- 1d\n│\n└── Agent Hook Retrieval\n    └── hooks/overseer_inbox run() \u003c-- skills/hooks_overseer_inbox/main.go:37\n        ├── OpenBoardStore() \u003c-- skills/hooks_overseer_inbox/main.go:59\n        ├── boardStore.Inbox() \u003c-- 1e\n        │   ├── Build SQL query with filters \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:100\n        │   └── QueryContext() \u003c-- 1f\n        │       └── SELECT WHERE recipient \u0026 status \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:103\n        ├── buildOverseerContext() \u003c-- skills/hooks_overseer_inbox/main.go:99\n        └── boardStore.MarkSurfaced() \u003c-- 1g\n            └── UPDATE status='surfaced' \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:208",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\n**Human-in-the-loop communication** during agent execution requires a way for humans to send messages to running agents and for those messages to be surfaced in the agent's context. The board message system solves this by providing **workspace-scoped messaging** with priority levels, status tracking (unread/surfaced/read), and automatic injection into agent context via hooks.\n\nThe problem: A human needs to tell a running Claude Code session \"stop working on feature X, focus on bug Y instead\" or \"review this before proceeding.\" Without this system, there's no way to interrupt or guide an agent mid-execution.\n\n## Details\n\n### Message Persistence\n\nMessages are stored in **board.db** SQLite database in the `board_messages` table [1d]. Each message has:\n- **workspace_id**: Scopes messages to a specific project\n- **recipient**: Target actor ID or \"*\" for broadcast\n- **priority**: 1 (highest) to 5 (lowest) for ordering\n- **status**: \"unread\" → \"surfaced\" → \"read\" → \"acked\"\n- **sender**: Who sent it (e.g., \"human\", actor ID)\n\n### Sending Flow\n\nThe **foxctl-mail** CLI command [1a] is the primary way humans send messages. It:\n1. Detects the workspace (via env vars or git root) [1b]\n2. Opens the board store for that workspace\n3. Calls `SendMessage()` which auto-generates a ULID and sets defaults [1c]\n4. Inserts the row with status=\"unread\" [1d]\n\n### Retrieval and Surfacing\n\nThe **hooks/overseer_inbox** hook runs during agent execution [1e]. It:\n1. Queries for `OnlyUnsurfaced` messages (status=\"unread\") to avoid re-injection\n2. Uses SQL filters: `WHERE workspace_id = ? AND (recipient = ? OR recipient = '*')` [1f]\n3. Orders by **priority ASC, created_at DESC** to show urgent messages first\n4. Injects message content into the agent's context as formatted markdown\n5. Marks displayed messages as \"surfaced\" [1g] so they won't be injected again\n\n### Status Lifecycle\n\n- **unread**: Just created, never shown to agent\n- **surfaced**: Injected into context by hook, but not explicitly acknowledged\n- **read**: Agent or user explicitly marked as read\n- **acked**: Agent confirmed receipt (for ack_required messages)\n\nThis three-stage status prevents **message spam** while preserving the distinction between \"AI saw it\" (surfaced) and \"human/agent explicitly handled it\" (read/acked)."
    },
