      "traceTextDiagram": "Agent Tool: mail.send\n├── Tool handler entry \u003c-- 2a\n│   ├── Extract args (recipient, subject, body) \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:177\n│   ├── Parse priority, kind, ack_required \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:198\n│   └── Open board store \u003c-- 2b\n│       └── OpenBoardStore(storageRoot) \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:47\n├── Construct BoardMessage \u003c-- 2c\n│   ├── Set WorkspaceID, TaskID, Sender \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:214\n│   └── Set Stream, Kind, Priority \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:216\n├── Persist message \u003c-- 2d\n│   └── store.SendMessage(ctx, msg) \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:62\n│       ├── Generate ULID if empty \u003c-- 2e\n│       ├── Set CreatedAt timestamp \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:66\n│       ├── Default status='unread' \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:70\n│       └── SQL INSERT execution \u003c-- 2f\n│           └── INSERT INTO board_messages \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:80\n│               (id, workspace_id, sender,\n│                recipient, priority, status...)\n└── Return success result \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:230\n    └── {message_id, sent_to, success: true} \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:231",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nAgents in foxctl need to **communicate with each other and with humans** during task execution. The `mail.send` tool enables this by allowing an agent to send **board messages**—workspace-scoped notifications with priority levels, acknowledgment tracking, and status management. These messages appear in recipient inboxes and can be surfaced by hooks into the agent's context, enabling human-in-the-loop workflows like \"pause and review this change\" or \"urgent: API design question.\"\n\n## Details\n\n### Tool Registration\n\nThe `mail.send` tool is registered in the agent's tool registry [2a] with a schema defining parameters: `recipient` (actor ID like \"overseer\" or \"agent:coder-1\"), `subject`, `body`, `kind` (instruction/info/alert/review_request), `priority` (1=highest, 5=lowest), and `ack_required` (boolean).\n\n### Message Construction\n\nWhen invoked, the tool handler extracts arguments from the tool call, applies defaults (priority=3, kind=info), and constructs a `BoardMessage` struct [2c] populated with:\n- **Workspace context**: `WorkspaceID` and `TaskID` from the agent's runtime config [2c]\n- **Sender identity**: `ActorID` from config becomes the `Sender` field\n- **Routing**: `Stream` defaults to \"coordination\" for workspace-wide messages\n- **Message content**: Subject, body, priority, kind, and ack flag from tool args\n\n### Persistence\n\nThe tool opens the **board store** [2b]—a SQLite database (`board.db`) in the storage root—and calls `SendMessage` [2d]. The store generates a **ULID** for the message ID [2e], sets `CreatedAt` timestamp, and defaults `Status` to \"unread\" [2f]. The message is then inserted into the `board_messages` table with all fields including workspace_id, sender, recipient, priority, and status.\n\n### Message Lifecycle\n\nOnce persisted, the message becomes queryable via the `Inbox` operation, which filters by workspace, recipient (including broadcast recipient \"*\"), and status. Messages progress through states: **unread** → **surfaced** (shown in context by hooks) → **read** (explicitly viewed) → **acked** (acknowledged). The priority field (1-5) controls ordering, with 1 being highest priority.\n\n### Return Value\n\nThe tool returns a success result [2a] containing the generated `message_id`, the `sent_to` recipient, and a success flag, allowing the agent to reference the message in subsequent operations or confirm delivery."
    },
