        },
        {
          "id": "3e",
          "path": "skills/mailbox/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 243,
          "lineContent": "_, _ = store.MarkRead(ctx, workspaceID, in.Inbox.ActorID, ids)",
          "title": "Mark as read",
          "description": "Best-effort UPDATE status='read' for displayed messages"
        },
        {
          "id": "3f",
          "path": "internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go",
          "lineNumber": 176,
          "lineContent": "res, err := s.db.ExecContext(ctx, query, args...)",
          "title": "SQL UPDATE",
          "description": "UPDATE board_messages SET status='read' WHERE status IN ('unread','surfaced')"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Inbox Query and Mark Read Flow (Trace 3)\n├── Mailbox Skill Entry\n│   └── run() with operation=\"inbox\" \u003c-- skills/mailbox/main.go:91\n│       └── store.Inbox(ctx, filter) \u003c-- 3a\n│           └── BoardStore.Inbox() \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:93\n│               ├── Build SQL query \u003c-- 3b\n│               │   ├── WHERE workspace_id AND recipient \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:100\n│               │   ├── Apply status filters \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:117\n│               │   └── ORDER BY priority, created_at \u003c-- 3c\n│               ├── Execute query \u003c-- 3d\n│               └── Return []BoardMessage \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:145\n└── Post-retrieval Processing\n    └── if !OnlyUnread \u003c-- skills/mailbox/main.go:237\n        └── store.MarkRead(ctx, ids) \u003c-- 3e\n            └── BoardStore.MarkRead() \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:149\n                └── SQL UPDATE status='read' \u003c-- 3f",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nAgents need to **coordinate within a workspace** by sending messages to each other and to human overseers. The board message system provides **priority-based inbox functionality** where messages can be filtered by recipient, task, and read status. This enables human-in-the-loop workflows where a human can send instructions to a running agent, and hooks can surface unread messages into the agent's context without re-injecting them forever.\n\nThe key problem: **how do you query messages efficiently** while tracking whether they've been seen (surfaced into context) versus explicitly read, and how do you prevent the same message from being injected into every agent turn?\n\n## Details\n\n### Message Storage and Querying\n\nBoard messages are stored in **`board_messages` table** in `board.db` with fields for workspace, recipient, priority (1=highest), status, subject, and body [3b]. The `Inbox` method builds a SQL query that filters by workspace and recipient, supporting wildcard `*` for broadcast messages [3b].\n\n### Status Lifecycle\n\nMessages progress through three states:\n- **`unread`**: newly created, never shown to agent\n- **`surfaced`**: injected into context by hooks but not explicitly acknowledged  \n- **`read`**: explicitly marked as read by user/tool\n\nThe query supports two filtering modes [3c]:\n- `OnlyUnsurfaced`: returns strictly `unread` messages (for hooks)\n- `OnlyUnread`: returns both `unread` and `surfaced` (for user queries)\n\n### Priority Ordering\n\nResults are **ordered by priority ascending** (1 first), then by `created_at` descending (newest first) [3c]. This ensures high-priority messages surface first while recent messages within the same priority appear at the top.\n\n### Preventing Re-injection\n\nAfter displaying messages, the skill conditionally calls `MarkRead` [3e]. The key distinction: if the query was `OnlyUnread=true` (checking for unread), it **skips marking as read** to allow hooks to see the same messages multiple times. Only non-filtering queries trigger the read status update [3e].\n\nThe `MarkRead` operation updates status from both `unread` and `surfaced` to `read` [3f], ensuring messages transition properly regardless of whether they were previously surfaced by a hook.\n\n### Execution Flow\n\nThe mailbox skill receives operation `\"inbox\"` with an `InboxFilter` containing `ActorID`, `TaskID`, `OnlyUnread`, and `Limit` [3a]. The store executes the filtered query [3d], returns a slice of `BoardMessage` structs [3d], and optionally marks them read based on the query type [3e]."
    },
