          "lineNumber": 316,
          "lineContent": "func (r *Registry) mailReserve(ctx context.Context, args map[string]any) (*models.CallToolResult, error) {",
          "title": "Tool handler entry",
          "description": "mail.reserve tool extracts paths, mode (exclusive/shared), ttl_seconds"
        },
        {
          "id": "4b",
          "path": "internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go",
          "lineNumber": 361,
          "lineContent": "conflicts, err := store.CheckConflicts(ctx, r.config.WorkspaceID, paths, r.config.ActorID, mode)",
          "title": "Check conflicts",
          "description": "Queries existing reservations to detect exclusive/shared conflicts"
        },
        {
          "id": "4c",
          "path": "internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go",
          "lineNumber": 282,
          "lineContent": "_, _ = s.db.ExecContext(ctx, `DELETE FROM file_reservations WHERE expires_at \u003c ?`, now)",
          "title": "Cleanup expired",
          "description": "Best-effort DELETE of expired reservations before conflict check"
        },
        {
          "id": "4d",
          "path": "internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go",
          "lineNumber": 313,
          "lineContent": "rows, err := s.db.QueryContext(ctx, query, args...)",
          "title": "Query conflicts",
          "description": "SELECT reservations WHERE path IN (?) AND holder != ? AND expires_at \u003e= ?"
        },
        {
          "id": "4e",
          "path": "internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go",
          "lineNumber": 386,
          "lineContent": "if err := store.Reserve(ctx, res); err != nil {",
          "title": "Create reservation",
          "description": "Inserts FileReservation if no conflicts found"
        },
        {
          "id": "4f",
          "path": "internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go",
          "lineNumber": 263,
          "lineContent": "_, err := s.db.ExecContext(ctx, `",
          "title": "SQL INSERT",
          "description": "INSERT file_reservations with ULID, path, holder, mode, expires_at"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "File Reservation Flow (Trace 4)\n├── Agent Tool Entry\n│   └── mail.reserve tool handler \u003c-- 4a\n│       └── Extract paths, mode, ttl from args \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:321\n│\n├── Conflict Detection Phase\n│   ├── store.CheckConflicts() call \u003c-- 4b\n│   │   ├── Cleanup expired reservations \u003c-- 4c\n│   │   │   └── DELETE WHERE expires_at \u003c now \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:282\n│   │   └── Query existing reservations \u003c-- 4d\n│   │       └── SELECT WHERE path IN (paths) \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:313\n│   │           AND holder != current_actor\n│   │           AND expires_at \u003e= now\n│   └── Return conflicts[] or empty \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:331\n│\n└── Reservation Creation Phase\n    ├── If no conflicts found \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:365\n    │   └── store.Reserve() call \u003c-- 4e\n    │       └── INSERT file_reservations \u003c-- 4f\n    │           ├── Generate ULID for id \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:254\n    │           ├── Set workspace_id, path, holder \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:377\n    │           ├── Set mode (exclusive/shared) \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:382\n    │           └── Set expires_at (now + ttl) \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:384\n    └── Return success or conflict error \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:392",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen multiple agents or processes work on the same codebase simultaneously, they can create **conflicting edits** to the same files. The file reservation system provides **advisory locks** that prevent this by allowing agents to declare their intent to modify specific files before making changes [4a]. This is similar to checking out a file in version control, but happens at runtime within a single workspace session.\n\nThe system uses **two reservation modes**: **exclusive** (only one holder can reserve) and **shared** (multiple holders can reserve for read-only access). Reservations automatically expire after a TTL (default 10 minutes) to prevent deadlocks if an agent crashes.\n\n## Details\n\n### Reservation Request Flow\n\nWhen an agent needs to modify files, it calls the `mail.reserve` tool with a list of paths [4a]. The tool first **checks for conflicts** by querying existing reservations in the `file_reservations` table [4b].\n\nBefore checking conflicts, the system performs **best-effort cleanup** of expired reservations by deleting rows where `expires_at \u003c now` [4c]. This prevents false conflicts from stale locks.\n\nThe conflict detection query [4d] looks for existing reservations on the same paths that:\n- Belong to a **different holder** (same actor can re-reserve)\n- Haven't expired yet (`expires_at \u003e= now`)\n- Would conflict with the requested mode (exclusive conflicts with everything; shared only conflicts with exclusive)\n\n### Conflict Resolution\n\nIf conflicts are found, the tool returns them to the agent with details about who holds the lock and when it expires [4b]. The agent can then decide to wait, request a different file, or escalate to human review.\n\nIf **no conflicts exist** [4e], the system creates a new reservation by inserting a row into `file_reservations` [4f]. Each reservation gets:\n- A **ULID** for unique identification [4f]\n- The **workspace_id** and **path** being reserved\n- The **holder** (actor ID making the reservation)\n- The **mode** (exclusive or shared)\n- An **expires_at** timestamp (current time + TTL)\n\nThe reservation is purely **advisory**—the system doesn't prevent file writes at the filesystem level. Agents are expected to check for conflicts before editing and respect existing reservations.\n\n### Storage Layer\n\nAll reservations live in the `board.db` SQLite database under the `file_reservations` table [4f]. The table is indexed on `(workspace_id, path)` for fast conflict lookups and on `expires_at` for efficient cleanup queries."
    },
