          "lineNumber": 448,
          "lineContent": "count, err := store.ReleaseByID(ctx, reservationIDs)",
          "title": "Release by IDs",
          "description": "Alternative deletion method using reservation ULIDs"
        },
        {
          "id": "5e",
          "path": "internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go",
          "lineNumber": 381,
          "lineContent": "res, err := s.db.ExecContext(ctx, query, args...)",
          "title": "SQL DELETE by ID",
          "description": "DELETE FROM file_reservations WHERE id IN (?) - no holder check"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "File Reservation Release Flow\n├── mail.release tool handler \u003c-- 5a\n│   ├── Extract paths[] or reservation_ids[] \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:406\n│   │   from tool arguments\n│   ├── Open board store (board.db) \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:431\n│   │\n│   ├── Release by paths branch\n│   │   ├── store.Release() call \u003c-- 5b\n│   │   │   └── Build DELETE query with \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:350\n│   │   │       workspace_id + holder + paths\n│   │   │       └── Execute DELETE \u003c-- 5c\n│   │   │           (WHERE workspace AND holder\n│   │   │            AND path IN (?))\n│   │\n│   └── Release by IDs branch\n│       ├── store.ReleaseByID() call \u003c-- 5d\n│       │   └── Build DELETE query with \u003c-- internal/storage/blackboard/board_store.go:379\n│       │       reservation IDs only\n│       │       └── Execute DELETE \u003c-- 5e\n│       │           (WHERE id IN (?))\n│       │\n│       └── Return released_count to agent \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/mail_tools.go:455",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen multiple agents or processes work on files in a shared workspace, **concurrent edits can corrupt work or create conflicts**. The file reservation system provides **advisory locks** that allow agents to declare their intent to modify specific files, preventing other agents from simultaneously editing the same files. These reservations are **time-limited** (with TTL) and stored in SQLite, so they survive process crashes and can be inspected or manually released.\n\nThe `mail.release` tool allows agents to **explicitly release their file reservations** when done editing, freeing the files for other agents to use [5a].\n\n## Details\n\n### Two Release Methods\n\nReservations can be released in two ways:\n\n1. **By file paths** - releases all reservations held by the current actor for specific files [5b]. This requires matching workspace ID, actor ID (holder), and file paths [5c].\n\n2. **By reservation IDs** - releases specific reservations using their ULID identifiers [5d]. This method doesn't check the holder, allowing cleanup of any reservation by ID [5e].\n\n### Implementation\n\nThe tool handler extracts either `paths[]` or `reservation_ids[]` from the tool arguments [5a]. It opens the board store (SQLite database at `board.db`) and calls the appropriate release method.\n\nFor path-based release, the SQL query is: `DELETE FROM file_reservations WHERE workspace_id = ? AND holder = ? AND path IN (?)` [5c]. This ensures agents can only release their own reservations.\n\nFor ID-based release, the query is simpler: `DELETE FROM file_reservations WHERE id IN (?)` [5e]. This is useful for administrative cleanup or when the reservation ID is known.\n\nBoth methods return the count of released reservations to the agent, allowing it to verify the operation succeeded.\n\n### Best Practices\n\nAgents should **release reservations as soon as editing is complete** to avoid blocking other agents unnecessarily. The TTL provides a safety net (default 10 minutes), but explicit release is preferred for responsive coordination."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "title": "Reactive mailbox message notification via SQLite trigger",
      "description": "Mailbox polling system: SQLite trigger fires on INSERT, watcher polls notify table, sends WakeUp to supervisor",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "6a",
          "path": "internal/storage/mailbox/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 64,
          "lineContent": "_, err = s.db.ExecContext(ctx, `",
          "title": "Message INSERT",
          "description": "INSERT INTO mailbox triggers mailbox_notify_trigger"
        },
        {
          "id": "6b",
          "path": "internal/actor/watcher.go",
          "lineNumber": 130,
          "lineContent": "trigger := `",
          "title": "Trigger definition",
          "description": "AFTER INSERT ON mailbox BEGIN INSERT INTO mailbox_notify (to_ns)"
        },
        {
          "id": "6c",
          "path": "internal/actor/watcher.go",
          "lineNumber": 163,
          "lineContent": "rows, err := w.db.QueryContext(ctx, `",
          "title": "Poll notify table",
          "description": "Watcher polls mailbox_notify every 50ms for new notifications"
        },
        {
          "id": "6d",
          "path": "internal/actor/watcher.go",
          "lineNumber": 189,
          "lineContent": "w.wakeUpCh \u003c- WakeUp{Namespace: ns, Timestamp: now}",
          "title": "Send WakeUp signal",
          "description": "Sends namespace wake-up to supervisor, one per namespace per poll"
        },
        {
          "id": "6e",
          "path": "internal/actor/supervisor.go",
          "lineNumber": 570,
          "lineContent": "case wake := \u003c-s.watcher.WakeUps():",
          "title": "Supervisor receives",
          "description": "Supervisor's runWatcher loop receives WakeUp from channel"
        },
        {
          "id": "6f",
          "path": "internal/actor/supervisor.go",
          "lineNumber": 571,
          "lineContent": "s.HandleWakeUp(s.ctx, wake)",
          "title": "Handle wake-up",
          "description": "Spawns goroutine to process wake-up if actor is idle"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Reactive Mailbox Message Notification Flow\n├── Message arrives in mailbox\n│   └── INSERT INTO mailbox \u003c-- 6a\n│       └── SQLite trigger fires\n│           └── AFTER INSERT trigger definition \u003c-- 6b\n│               └── INSERT INTO mailbox_notify \u003c-- internal/actor/watcher.go:134\n├── Watcher polling loop (50ms interval) \u003c-- internal/actor/watcher.go:143\n│   └── SELECT FROM mailbox_notify \u003c-- 6c\n│       └── Group by namespace \u003c-- internal/actor/watcher.go:174\n│           └── Send WakeUp to channel \u003c-- 6d\n└── Supervisor receives notification\n    ├── WakeUp received from channel \u003c-- 6e\n    └── HandleWakeUp() spawns goroutine \u003c-- 6f\n        └── Check if actor is idle \u003c-- internal/actor/supervisor.go:373\n            └── Poll mailbox for message \u003c-- internal/actor/supervisor.go:383",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nAgents in foxctl need to react to incoming messages immediately rather than polling continuously. The problem: **how do you wake up an idle actor when a new message arrives without burning CPU on constant polling?** The solution uses SQLite triggers to create a reactive notification system that provides ~50ms latency while keeping actors idle when there's no work.\n\n## Details\n\n### SQLite Trigger-Based Notifications\n\nWhen a message is inserted into the `mailbox` table [6a], a SQLite trigger automatically fires [6b] and inserts a notification row into `mailbox_notify` with the recipient namespace [6b]. This happens **atomically within the same transaction** as the message insert, ensuring no messages are missed.\n\n### Watcher Polling Loop\n\nThe `Watcher` runs a background goroutine that polls the `mailbox_notify` table every 50ms [6c]. This is far more efficient than polling the mailbox itself because:\n- The notify table is tiny (just namespace strings)\n- Multiple messages to the same namespace produce only one wake-up signal\n- Notifications are deleted after processing, keeping the table small\n\nWhen notifications are found, the watcher groups them by namespace [6c] and sends one `WakeUp` signal per namespace to a buffered channel [6d].\n\n### Supervisor Wake-Up Handling\n\nThe `Supervisor` listens on the wake-up channel in its main loop [6e]. When a `WakeUp` arrives, it spawns a goroutine to handle it [6f], but only if:\n1. The actor for that namespace is registered\n2. The actor is currently **idle** (not already processing a message)\n3. No other goroutine is already handling this namespace\n\nThis prevents unbounded goroutine spawning under high message volume while maintaining the **sequential processing contract**: each actor processes one message at a time.\n\n### Atomic Message Claiming\n\nOnce the actor is confirmed idle, the supervisor calls `mailbox.Poll()` [6f → 7a] which uses a **transaction with lease semantics** to atomically claim the message. The wake-up is just a signal—the actual message consumption happens through the existing Poll/Ack mechanism, preserving crash safety."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "title": "Polling and acknowledging mailbox messages with lease",
      "description": "Mailbox polling system: Atomic lease-based message claim, delivery to actor, and acknowledgment",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "7a",
          "path": "internal/actor/supervisor.go",
          "lineNumber": 383,
          "lineContent": "msg, err := s.mailbox.Poll(ctx, wake.Namespace, s.leaseTimeout)",
          "title": "Poll for message",
          "description": "Supervisor polls mailbox if actor is idle (sequential processing)"
        },
        {
          "id": "7b",
          "path": "internal/storage/mailbox/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 83,
          "lineContent": "tx, err := s.db.BeginTx(ctx, nil)",
          "title": "Begin transaction",
          "description": "Poll uses transaction to atomically claim message with lease"
        },
        {
          "id": "7c",
          "path": "internal/storage/mailbox/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 92,
          "lineContent": "rows, err := tx.QueryContext(ctx, `",
          "title": "SELECT visible",
          "description": "SELECT WHERE to_ns=? AND visible_at \u003c= ? ORDER BY ts LIMIT 1"
        },
        {
          "id": "7d",
          "path": "internal/storage/mailbox/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 128,
          "lineContent": "res, err := tx.ExecContext(ctx, `",
          "title": "UPDATE lease",
          "description": "UPDATE visible_at to future time, increment attempt for lease"
        },
        {
          "id": "7e",
          "path": "internal/actor/supervisor.go",
          "lineNumber": 413,
          "lineContent": "err := actor.OnMailReceived(ctx, msg)",
          "title": "Deliver to actor",
          "description": "Calls actor's message handler with leased message"
        },
        {
          "id": "7f",
          "path": "internal/actor/supervisor.go",
          "lineNumber": 431,
          "lineContent": "if err := s.mailbox.Ack(ctx, msg.ID); err != nil {",
          "title": "Acknowledge message",
          "description": "On success, ack deletes message; on error, nack extends lease"
        },
        {
          "id": "7g",
          "path": "internal/storage/mailbox/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 172,
          "lineContent": "res, err := s.db.ExecContext(ctx, `DELETE FROM mailbox WHERE id = ?`, messageID)",
          "title": "SQL DELETE",
          "description": "Ack removes message from mailbox table permanently"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Mailbox Message Polling \u0026 Acknowledgment Flow\n├── Supervisor receives WakeUp signal \u003c-- internal/actor/supervisor.go:570\n│   └── HandleWakeUp() spawns goroutine \u003c-- internal/actor/supervisor.go:571\n│       ├── Check actor is idle \u003c-- internal/actor/supervisor.go:373\n│       └── Poll mailbox atomically \u003c-- 7a\n│           └── MailboxAdapter.Poll() \u003c-- internal/actor/mailbox_adapter.go:62\n│               └── Store.Poll() begins transaction \u003c-- 7b\n│                   ├── SELECT visible messages \u003c-- 7c\n│                   ├── UPDATE visible_at (lease) \u003c-- 7d\n│                   └── COMMIT transaction \u003c-- internal/storage/mailbox/store.go:164\n├── Deliver message to actor\n│   └── actor.OnMailReceived(msg) \u003c-- 7e\n│       └── Actor processes message\n│           └── Returns success/error\n└── Acknowledge or Nack message \u003c-- internal/actor/supervisor.go:425\n    ├── On success: mailbox.Ack() \u003c-- 7f\n    │   └── DELETE FROM mailbox \u003c-- 7g\n    └── On error: mailbox.Nack() \u003c-- internal/actor/supervisor.go:465\n        └── UPDATE visible_at (retry later) \u003c-- internal/storage/mailbox/store.go:188",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nAgents need to communicate asynchronously without blocking or polling. The **mailbox polling system** solves this by storing messages in SQLite and using **database triggers** to notify a supervisor when new messages arrive. This enables **reactive, event-driven actors** that wake up only when work is available, rather than constantly polling an empty queue.\n\nThe system guarantees **at-least-once delivery** through lease-based message claiming: when an actor polls for work, it atomically claims a message with a TTL lease [7b, 7c, 7d]. If processing fails or the actor crashes, the lease expires and the message becomes visible again for retry.\n\n## Details\n\n### Reactive Notification Flow\n\nWhen a message is inserted into the `mailbox` table [6a], a SQLite trigger automatically inserts a row into `mailbox_notify` [6b]. A **Watcher** polls this notify table every 50ms [6c], groups notifications by namespace, and sends **WakeUp signals** to the supervisor [6d, 6e, 6f]. This provides ~50ms latency while keeping the mailbox durable.\n\n### Atomic Message Claiming\n\nThe supervisor receives a WakeUp and checks if the target actor is idle (enforcing **sequential processing** per actor). It then calls `Poll()` [7a], which begins a transaction [7b], selects messages where `visible_at \u003c= now` [7c], and updates `visible_at` to a future timestamp (the lease) [7d]. The transaction commit makes the claim atomic—only one poller wins the race.\n\n### Processing and Acknowledgment\n\nThe supervisor delivers the message to the actor via `OnMailReceived()` [7e]. On success, it calls `Ack()` [7f] which **deletes the message** from the mailbox [7g]. On failure, it calls `Nack()` which extends the `visible_at` timestamp, making the message invisible temporarily before becoming available for retry.\n\n### Adapter Pattern\n\nThe `MailboxAdapter` wraps the storage layer [8a, 8b] and converts between `agent.Message` (storage format with `json.RawMessage` payload) and `actor.Message` (supervisor format with typed fields) [8d, 8e]. This decouples the actor system from storage implementation details."
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "title": "Mailbox adapter converts between storage and actor formats",
      "description": "Mailbox polling system: Adapter pattern wraps storage layer, converts agent.Message to actor.Message",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "8a",
          "path": "internal/actor/mailbox_adapter.go",
          "lineNumber": 62,
          "lineContent": "func (a *MailboxAdapter) Poll(ctx context.Context, namespace string, leaseTimeout time.Duration) (*Message, error) {",
          "title": "Adapter Poll",
          "description": "Wraps mailbox.Store to provide MailboxStore interface for supervisor"
        },
        {
          "id": "8b",
          "path": "internal/actor/mailbox_adapter.go",
          "lineNumber": 64,
          "lineContent": "messages, err := a.store.Poll(ctx, namespace, leaseTimeout, 1)",
          "title": "Call storage Poll",
          "description": "Delegates to storage layer, requests maxMessages=1"
        },
        {
          "id": "8c",
          "path": "internal/storage/mailbox/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 75,
          "lineContent": "func (s *sqlStore) Poll(ctx context.Context, agentNS string, leaseDuration time.Duration, maxMessages int) ([]agent.Message, error) {",
          "title": "Storage Poll",
          "description": "Returns []agent.Message with Payload as json.RawMessage"
        },
        {
          "id": "8d",
          "path": "internal/actor/mailbox_adapter.go",
          "lineNumber": 72,
          "lineContent": "return a.toActorMessage(\u0026messages[0]), nil",
          "title": "Convert message",
          "description": "Transforms agent.Message to actor.Message for supervisor"
        },
        {
          "id": "8e",
          "path": "internal/actor/mailbox_adapter.go",
          "lineNumber": 92,
          "lineContent": "return \u0026Message{",
          "title": "Message mapping",
          "description": "Maps Type→Subject, Payload→Body, Timestamp→CreatedAt, TTLMS→ExpiresAt"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Mailbox Message Polling Flow\n├── Supervisor Layer\n│   └── MailboxAdapter.Poll() \u003c-- 8a\n│       ├── calls storage with maxMessages=1 \u003c-- 8b\n│       └── converts response format \u003c-- 8d\n│           └── toActorMessage() mapping \u003c-- 8e\n│               └── Type→Subject, Payload→Body \u003c-- internal/actor/mailbox_adapter.go:96\n│\n└── Storage Layer\n    └── sqlStore.Poll() \u003c-- 8c\n        ├── BeginTx() for atomic claim \u003c-- internal/storage/mailbox/store.go:83\n        ├── SELECT WHERE visible_at \u003c= now \u003c-- internal/storage/mailbox/store.go:92\n        ├── UPDATE visible_at for lease \u003c-- internal/storage/mailbox/store.go:128\n        ├── Commit transaction \u003c-- internal/storage/mailbox/store.go:164\n        └── returns []agent.Message \u003c-- internal/storage/mailbox/store.go:168\n            └── (json.RawMessage payload) \u003c-- internal/storage/mailbox/store.go:398",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe actor system needs to deliver messages from a **durable SQLite mailbox** to in-memory actors, but the storage layer uses `agent.Message` (with `json.RawMessage` payloads and Unix timestamps) while the supervisor expects `actor.Message` (with byte slices and `time.Time` fields). The **MailboxAdapter** [8a] bridges this impedance mismatch, converting between the two formats so the supervisor can work with a clean interface without knowing about storage details.\n\n## Details\n\n### Adapter Pattern\n\nThe `MailboxAdapter` wraps `mailbox.Store` and implements the `MailboxStore` interface expected by the supervisor. When the supervisor calls `Poll()` [8a], the adapter delegates to the underlying storage's `Poll()` method [8b], which returns `[]agent.Message` [8c].\n\n### Message Conversion\n\nThe storage layer returns messages with fields like `Type` (message type enum), `Payload` (JSON bytes), and `Timestamp` (Unix seconds) [8c]. The adapter's `toActorMessage()` function [8d] transforms this into `actor.Message` by:\n- Mapping `Type` → `Subject` (string conversion) [8e]\n- Mapping `Payload` → `Body` (raw bytes)\n- Converting `Timestamp` + `TTLMS` → `CreatedAt` and `ExpiresAt` (`time.Time` objects)\n\n### Lease Semantics\n\nThe storage layer handles the **atomic message claim** with a transaction [8b]: it queries for visible messages, updates `visible_at` to a future timestamp (the lease), and commits. The adapter simply requests `maxMessages=1` and returns the single claimed message to the supervisor, which then delivers it to the actor for processing.\n\nThis separation allows the storage layer to focus on durability and atomicity while the supervisor works with idiomatic Go types."
    }
  ],
  "description": "Three coordination systems: (1) Board messages for workspace-scoped human-agent communication with priority/status tracking, (2) File reservations for preventing concurrent edits, and (3) Mailbox polling for durable inter-actor messaging with reactive SQLite triggers. Key entry points: human message sending [1a], agent tool usage [2a], file reservation [4a], and reactive message polling [6c].",
  "mermaidDiagram": "graph TB\n    subgraph BoardMsgs[\"Board Messages\"]\n        style BoardMsgs fill:#fcc2d7\n        1a[\"1a: CLI entry point\"]\n        1c[\"1c: Send message\"]\n        1d[\"1d: SQL INSERT\"]\n        1e[\"1e: Hook queries inbox\"]\n        1g[\"1g: Mark surfaced\"]\n        2a[\"2a: Tool handler\"]\n        2d[\"2d: Persist message\"]\n        2f[\"2f: SQL INSERT\"]\n        3a[\"3a: Query inbox\"]\n        3d[\"3d: Execute query\"]\n        3f[\"3f: SQL UPDATE read\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph FileRes[\"File Reservations\"]\n        style FileRes fill:#eebefa\n        4a[\"4a: Tool reserve\"]\n        4b[\"4b: Check conflicts\"]\n        4d[\"4d: Query conflicts\"]\n        4f[\"4f: SQL INSERT\"]\n        5a[\"5a: Tool release\"]\n        5c[\"5c: SQL DELETE path\"]\n        5e[\"5e: SQL DELETE ID\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph BoardStore[\"BoardStore Hub\"]\n        style BoardStore fill:#ffec99\n        BS[\"board.db\u003cbr/\u003eboard_messages\u003cbr/\u003efile_reservations\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph MailboxPoll[\"Mailbox Polling\"]\n        style MailboxPoll fill:#99e9f2\n        6a[\"6a: Message INSERT\"]\n        6b[\"6b: Trigger fires\"]\n        6c[\"6c: Watcher polls\"]\n        6d[\"6d: WakeUp signal\"]\n        6e[\"6e: Supervisor receives\"]\n        6f[\"6f: Handle wake-up\"]\n        7a[\"7a: Poll message\"]\n        7b[\"7b: Begin transaction\"]\n        7d[\"7d: UPDATE lease\"]\n        7e[\"7e: Deliver to actor\"]\n        7f[\"7f: Acknowledge\"]\n        7g[\"7g: SQL DELETE\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph MailboxStore[\"Mailbox Hub\"]\n        style MailboxStore fill:#a5d8ff\n        MS[\"mailbox.db\u003cbr/\u003emailbox table\u003cbr/\u003emailbox_notify\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph Adapter[\"Message Adapter\"]\n        style Adapter fill:#d0bfff\n        8a[\"8a: Adapter Poll\"]\n        8b[\"8b: Call storage\"]\n        8c[\"8c: Storage Poll\"]\n        8d[\"8d: Convert message\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph Tools[\"Agent Tools\"]\n        style Tools fill:#b2f2bb\n        SEND[\"mail.send\"]\n        RESERVE[\"mail.reserve\"]\n        RELEASE[\"mail.release\"]\n        INBOX[\"mail.inbox\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph Hooks[\"Hooks\"]\n        style Hooks fill:#ffd8a8\n        OVERSEER[\"overseer_inbox\"]\n        FILEGUARD[\"file_guard\"]\n    end\n    \n    %% Board Messages flow\n    1a --\u003e|opens| BS\n    1c --\u003e|persists| BS\n    1d --\u003e|inserts| BS\n    \n    2a --\u003e|is| SEND\n    2d --\u003e|persists| BS\n    2f --\u003e|inserts| BS\n    \n    3a --\u003e|is| INBOX\n    3d --\u003e|queries| BS\n    3f --\u003e|updates| BS\n    \n    %% File Reservations flow\n    4a --\u003e|is| RESERVE\n    4b --\u003e|queries| BS\n    4d --\u003e|checks| BS\n    4f --\u003e|inserts| BS\n    \n    5a --\u003e|is| RELEASE\n    5c --\u003e|deletes| BS\n    5e --\u003e|deletes| BS\n    \n    %% Hooks consume board messages\n    1e --\u003e|is| OVERSEER\n    1g --\u003e|marks| BS\n    FILEGUARD --\u003e|reads| BS\n    \n    %% Mailbox polling flow\n    6a --\u003e|triggers| 6b\n    6b --\u003e|fires| 6c\n    6c --\u003e|polls| MS\n    6d --\u003e|sends| 6e\n    6e --\u003e|routes| 6f\n    6f --\u003e|calls| 7a\n    \n    %% Poll and ack flow\n    7a --\u003e|begins| 7b\n    7b --\u003e|claims| MS\n    7d --\u003e|leases| MS\n    7e --\u003e|delivers| 7f\n    7f --\u003e|acks| 7g\n    7g --\u003e|deletes| MS\n    \n    %% Adapter bridges\n    8a --\u003e|wraps| 8b\n    8b --\u003e|calls| 8c\n    8c --\u003e|returns| 8d\n    8d --\u003e|maps| 8e\n    \n    %% Supervisor uses adapter\n    6f --\u003e|uses| 8a\n    8c --\u003e|queries| MS"
}